ck" content="true" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:android:url" content="meetup://" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:ios:url" content="meetup://" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:web:url" content="https://www.meetup.com/" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:site" content="@meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:image" content="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/next/images/shared/meetup-flyer.png" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:description" content="Find Meetup events and groups so you can do more of what matters to you and meet people near you who share your interests." data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:id:iphone" content="375990038" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:name:iphone" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:id:ipad" content="375990038" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:name:ipad" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:id:googleplay" content="com.meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:name:googleplay" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow" data-next-head=""/><link rel="canonical" href="https://www.meetup.com/find/" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://secure-content.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://secure-content.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://www.googletagmanager.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://www.googletagmanager.com" data-next-head=""/><script type="application/ld+json" data-next-head="">[{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Qi Gong for 60+","url":"https://www.meetup.com/chi-of-thee-meetup-group/events/316651501/","description":"### Inviting Adults 60+ to Start Your Healing Journey with Pureland Qi Gong — On the Danforth\n\n**with Generational Qi Gong Master Teresa Yeung**\nAfter a lifetime of caring for your family, friends, and others, **it's time to care for yourself.**\nAt 69, Master Teresa Yeung understands that staying active and taking care of our body, mind, and spirit becomes increasingly important as we grow older.\nThis is your time to **nurture yourself, keep moving, and thrive in the years ahead.**\nThrough the gentle practice of **Pureland Qi Gong**, you will learn simple movements, breathing, and relaxation practices designed to support your body's natural balance, circulation, flexibility, and vitality.\n\n### Keep Your Body Moving. Keep Your Spirit Thriving.\n\nQi Gong offers a gentle way to continue being active while giving yourself time to slow down, breathe, and reconnect.\nYou will explore practices that can help you:\n\n* **Keep the body gently moving**\n* Support flexibility, balance, and coordination\n* Encourage relaxation and mindful breathing\n* Cultivate and circulate Qi (energy)\n* Develop greater awareness of your body\n* Create a regular practice for your own well-being\n\n**And you can practice both standing and seated.** You don't have to be on your feet for the entire class.\n\n### Your Next Chapter Can Be About You\n\nYou have spent much of your life taking care of others.\nNow, take one hour for **yourself**.\nJoin Teresa Yeung and other adults 60+ for a welcoming introduction to **Pureland Qi Gong** and discover a gentle practice you can continue to enjoy as you move forward in life.\n**You are never too old to start something new.**\n\n## A Special Introductory Class\n\nThis 1-hour class is an opportunity to **experience Qi Gong with Teresa before deciding whether you would like to continue**.\nIf there is sufficient interest, a **4-week Qi Gong program for adults 60+** may be offered following these introductory sessions.\nThere is **no obligation to register for the 4-week program**. Come simply to experience the class and see if Qi Gong is right for you.\n\n## 📍 In-Person Class — Toronto\n\n**Room 212 Danforth Avenue**\n**2nd floor of Carrot Common**\n**Toronto, Ontario M4K 1P1**\n\n### 📍 **Choose your Class**\n\n**Wednesday, October 14, 2026 (register here)**\n🕥 **10:30 AM – 11:30 AM**\n**OR**\n**Thursday, October 22, 2026**\n🕑 **2:00 PM – 3:00 PM**\n**(register separately: https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/qi-gong-for-60-tickets-2001885090194?aff=ebemoffollowpublishemail&ref=eemail&utm_campaign=following_published_event&utm_content=follow_notification&utm_medium=email&utm_source=eventbrite)**\n\nPlease register for the date and time that works best for you. **Each class is a separate event.**\n\n### 💰 **Introductory Class Fee**\n\n**$20 + 13% HST = $22.60 total**\nThe introductory class fee is **$22.60 per person, including HST**.\n\n## What to Bring\n\n* Comfortable clothing\n* Water\n* A willingness to relax, breathe and enjoy the experience\n\nPlease arrive **10–15 minutes early** so you have time to settle in before the class begins.\n\n## Meet Your Teacher — Teresa Yeung\n\n**Generational Qi Gong Master Teresa Yeung** is the founder of Pureland International Qi Gong in Canada and a successor in the lineage of Grandmaster Weizhao Wu.\nWith more than **30 years of experience teaching Qi Gong internationally**, Teresa has shared Qi Gong with people from many different backgrounds and age groups.\nShe is the creator of **Wu's Eye Qi Gong®, Heart Chi Gong™ and the Hidden Pearl Series for Women**, and is a **3-time #1 internationally bestselling author**.\nAt 69, Teresa is especially interested in sharing Qi Gong with people in her own generation — helping them discover simple ways to keep moving, breathing and cultivating greater balance in everyday life.\nPurelandQiGong.com\n\n#carrotcommon\n#torontoqigongtaichi\n#seniors","startDate":"2026-10-14T14:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Chi of Thee Meetup Group","url":"https://www.meetup.com/chi-of-thee-meetup-group/"},"performer":"Chi of Thee Meetup Group"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"♠️ $375 NLH Tournament – $25,000 Guaranteed ♠️","url":"https://www.meetup.com/lodge401pokerclub/events/316764679/","description":"Join us **Wednesday, October 14th at 2:00 PM** for another exciting **No Limit Hold’em tournament** at **Lodge 401**. Great action, professional dealers, and a premium poker atmosphere.\n\n💰 **Tournament Details:**\n• **$375 NLH Re-entry Tournament ( includes add-on)**\n• **$25,000 Guaranteed Prize Pool**\n• **30,000 Starting Stack ( include add-on)**\n• **25 Minute Blind Levels**\n**• Late registration until end of level 6 break**\n\n♣️ **Cash Games Available**\nAfter the first break we will open cash tables:\n• **1-3 NLH**\n• **2-2-5 PLO**\nPerfect for players who bust early or want to jump into cash action.\n\n📍 **Location:**\n1645 Warden Ave\n📞 **Reserve your seat:**\n647-401-7768\n\nLodge 401 offers a premium poker experience with professional dealers, comfortable tables, and a great community of players. Seats fill up quickly, so **reserve your spot early.**\n\n♠️ **See you at the tables!** ♠️","startDate":"2026-10-14T18:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Lodge 401","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1645 Warden Ave, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Lodge 401 Poker Club","url":"https://www.meetup.com/lodge401pokerclub/"},"performer":"Lodge 401 Poker Club"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"FREE Spanish, English, and French Oral Conversational Class!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/free-frenchspanish-classes-for-adults/events/316699573/","description":"\\*These classes are not a language exchange, but instead are meant to be a step in between so that students feel confident maintaining in depth and grammatically correct oral conversations outside of class\\*\n\n\\***Meetup event numbers only tend to show new students registering and do not include returning students attending class.** **Per class, there is an average of 7 students.** The first 2 classes are free and then only cost between $18 and $35 depending on which type of class you want to continue with\\*\n\nThese French, English (For Spanish and French speakers only), and Spanish classes are primarily meant for adults who are travellers, or who are planning to live in a French, English, or Spanish-speaking country. The classes are primarily oral-based through guided conversations. They will teach you how to handle conversations in situations such as **\"Going to the Convenience Store\"**, **\"Making Plans\"**, **\"Negotiating Prices\"**, and **\"Going out for a Drink\"**. To ensure that students get used to using the language automatically, students will learn to maintain contextual conversations with timing before moving on to the next lesson. Call (647)787-9953, e-mail us info@monkeylingo.ca, or visit monkeylingo.ca for more information! **Online and private classes are also available!**\n\nNo other language classes are as conversational as these ones. We guarantee it! Cheap parking can be found using the \"Spot Hero\" app.","startDate":"2026-10-14T20:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"600 Bay St.","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"600 Bay St., Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Free Conversational Spanish, English, French Class 4 Adults!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/free-frenchspanish-classes-for-adults/"},"performer":"Free Conversational Spanish, English, French Class 4 Adults!"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Creative Code Toronto work session","url":"https://www.meetup.com/creative-code-toronto/events/316641588/","description":"Join us for a Toronto meetup of creative coders! Instead of our usual show-and-tell, this will be a **work session!** If you're looking for some motivation to tinker on a creative project, now's your chance!\n\n**What is creative code?** *Creative coding* refers to anything with an artistic component that uses code as a medium. We welcome artists who use code (for visuals, audio, poetry, or whatever else), designers, animators, toolmakers, researchers, or just enjoyers and people looking to learn more!\n\n**Location:** Impact Kitchen on Queens Quay (88 Queens Quay W, Toronto, ON M5J 0B6)\n\n**Join our discord** if you want to talk to everyone before/after the event, or have any suggestions for things you'd like to see or do! [https://discord.gg/ux9txXPsdJ](https://discord.gg/ux9txXPsdJ)","startDate":"2026-10-14T21:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"88 Queens Quay W","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"88 Queens Quay W, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Creative Code Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/creative-code-toronto/"},"performer":"Creative Code Toronto"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Magic the Gathering: Going Commander","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-gaymers/events/316699752/","description":"Every Wednesday Night!\nFree Magic The Gathering Commander games at Hairy Tarantula, hosted by Toronto Gaymers!\n\nPlease note: Masks are required in store!\n\nFor more information and to RSVP please over to harryt.com/events","startDate":"2026-10-14T21:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Hairy Tarantula","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"CA","streetAddress":"3456 Yonge Street, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Gaymers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-gaymers/"},"performer":"Toronto Gaymers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"The Future of Wellbeing: AI, Community & Social Impact","url":"https://www.meetup.com/gdg-toronto/events/316389242/","description":"Register here: https://www.eventbrite.ca/e/the-future-of-wellbeing-ai-community-social-impact-tickets-1997859089317?utm_source=ig&utm_medium=social&utm_content=link_in_bio&fbclid=PAcGRvZgJleHRuA2FlbQIxMQBzcnRjBmFwcF9pZA85MzY2MTk3NDMzOTI0NTkAAad9JE43Cv4asJwzLwmAkV5UH94sl9eJwjPGVPLPRLCUuBLTGMNoB7aCPW61-A_aem_eqTb0M6UTv4G97JZPcFxPw\n\n**Overview**\nWhat does it mean to build AI in service of wellbeing? A one-day forum on tech, climate, mental health, community & social impact.\n*A Community Panel & Networking*\nAn evening forum on what it means to build technology in service of wellbeing.\nAs AI reshapes how we live, work, and care for one another, one question matters more than ever: what does it mean to build and adopt technology in service of holistic wellbeing — human, community, and societal — in the Canadian context?\nThe Mindful Impact Forum brings together nonprofit leaders, founders, technologists, youth, and changemakers for a focused day of conversation and practice. We move deliberately from the human to the technical: first setting the foundation of what wellbeing truly means, then turning to how we build and adopt AI responsibly in service of it.\nAfter launching our forum series in Vancouver this past March, we're bringing it to Toronto for a single, focused edition — in partnership with Google Developer Groups and The Dais, TMU.\n\n### **What you'll experience**\n\n* A flagship day of remarks, a keynote, and an opening panel on wellbeing\n* A creatively facilitated community forum — real cross-sector dialogue\n* A hands-on AI & technology for social impact workshop\n* Practical tools for leadership, resilience, and innovation you can use the next morning\n* A genuinely cross-sector room: founders, youth leaders, community builders, and changemakers\n\n### **The program**\n\nSession 1 — Framing & Community Panel: What Wellbeing Means\nSession 2 — AI and Responsible Innovation: From Principles to Practice\nSession 3 — Finding our Wisdom Way Forward: Future Community Wellbeing & Leadership\n\n## Event Details\n\n**📍 Location:** The Sandbox, TMU (341 Yonge St 3rd floor, Toronto, ON M5B 1S1)\n**📅 Date:** Oct 14, Wednesday 2026\n**⏰ Time:** 6 PM - 9:00 PM (Door open 5:30 PM)\n**🎫 Ticket — FREE -$50**\nAll proceeds support Wisdomway Impact’s mental wellbeing initiatives. Student & Youth (under 25, limited spots) FREE\n\n**Speakers**\n\n1. **AJ Kim** is a social entrepreneur, global impact practitioner, dedicated to building spaces where inner development and collective change meet. Her work spans leadership development, youth empowerment, and community wellbeing initiatives in Asia, Africa, and Canada, grounded in field experiences, dialogue, and systems thinking. Through forums, education programs, and partnerships, she explores how mental wellbeing can become a foundation for stronger communities, sustainable leadership, and long-term social impact.\n2. **Alejandro Castellanos** Toronto-based AI Systems Architect, Alejandro builds trustworthy AI technologies for community resilience, public-interest intelligence, and human-centred care. His work emphasizes evidence, human oversight, and technology that strengthens—not replaces—human judgment.\n3. **Camara Chambers** (*Director of Learning and Events, The Dais at TMU)* Named one of 100 Black Women in Canada to Watch and a national leader by The Philanthropist Journal, Camara has spent her career where equity meets civic engagement — leading a national policy program for Europe's largest LGBTQ charity, and serving as Executive Director of Volunteer Toronto, Canada's largest volunteer centre. At the Dais she builds community partnerships and designs leadership programs for Canada's next generation of leaders, and she founded Let's Hike T.O., which has introduced over 1,300 people to the trails. She brings the question that keeps the whole session honest: responsible *for whom?*\n4. **Carolyn Shaw** is the Co-Founder, President and Chief Creative Officer of Humanity, an independent, Black-owned and female-led agency built for changemakers. With more than 20 years of experience in marketing, branding and design, she helps purpose-driven organizations turn bold ambitions into ideas, experiences and campaigns that move people. Carolyn believes the strongest organizations are built by keeping people—their needs, dignity and lived experiences—at the centre of how we lead, communicate and create change. Her work spans health, education, culture, sustainability and the nonprofit sector, bringing strategy and creativity together to make complex issues more human and meaningful. A lifelong learner and advocate for purpose-led leadership, Carolyn is especially interested in how organizations can pursue progress without losing sight of the people that progress is meant to serve.\n5. **Danielle (dane) Cadhit** is an experience designer, story weaver, facilitator, and lifelong observer of patterns. At Coralus, she crafts experiences that invite people to connect more deeply, see and do things differently, and (re)imagine new possibilities.Her curiosity tends to live in the spaces between things: between people and ideas, work and life, structure and emergence, the inner world and the communities we build around us. Lately, she has been especially interested in what happens when we stop treating ourselves like something to optimize, and instead pay more attention to the rhythms, seasons, relationships, and conditions that shape how we actually live, work, gather, and create.\n6. **Hilary Van Welter** is CEO (Chief Exploration Officer) at Ascentia, Coralus Transformation Architect, and Associate Steward at Bounce Beyond. She has spent a lifetime exploring how life, people, organizations, communities and nature flourish, evolve and bring new possibilities into being. Her perspective has been shaped by decades of looking at these questions from many angles, across government, business, social innovation, community and systems transformation. Her work lives at the intersection of strategy, imagination and living systems, with a particular curiosity about the relationships and conditions that reimagine even the term wellbeing beyond the individual into community and society. She brings the wisdom of a long trajectory, a deep trust in life’s intelligence, and an ability to sense patterns and possibilities while they are still emerging.\n7. **Jake Hirsch-Allen** (*Director of Partnerships, The Dais at TMU)* Jake works at the intersection of inclusive technology, ethical data, and responsible AI. He built public-private partnerships in workforce development and higher education at LinkedIn, co-founded Lighthouse Labs, and advises impact investors, public-sector leaders, and startups on responsible tech and AI governance. A former intellectual property and international criminal lawyer who clerked at the Supreme Court of Israel, he can speak to the ethics, the policy, and the build of AI all at once — and here, he opens the questions the demos will have to answer.\n8. **Katie Choi (she/her)** is the Lead of Community Education at HF Care and a registered social worker with experience supporting diverse communities across the mental health, developmental services, and settlement sectors. Drawing on both her professional background and her lived experience as an immigrant and the daughter of immigrant parents, Katie is passionate about exploring how culture, migration, and family dynamics shape holistic wellness. Through her work, she supports front-line workers in building culturally responsive, trauma-informed, and strengths-based approaches to service delivery.\n9. **Kritima Kukreja** Technology professional and mobile developer, Founder of Synk Tech AI. Specialized in creating smart agents, chatbots and automations that scales for the client’s needs. A former experienced developer in well-known companies such as IBM, MicroSoft, Bank of America, and Google. Kritima builds user-focused digital experiences and explores the intersection of AI, mobile technology, and emerging digital tools. She is also an active member of Toronto’s tech community, supporting and mentoring fellow builders.\n10. **Swelen Andari** is the Director of Strategy, Climate Resilience & Youth Mental Health at the Centre for Addiction and Mental Health (CAMH). She leads a research and systems change initiative to address climate distress, climate action, and active hope for youth. Swelen leads the CAMH Mental Health & Climate Response Initiative, an organization-wide effort addressing climate-related mental health impacts. Trained as a Creative Arts Therapist and with a background in systems thinking, and implementation science, she has over a decade of experience in system-level initiatives to improve access, service design, prevention, and youth leadership in Ontario’s child/youth mental health system. For several years, Swelen was involved in local and national climate justice organizing, including collaborating with Climate Justice Toronto, supporting the 350’s Our Time Campaign, and co-designing a social movement organization committed to advancing equitable climate solution, good work and dignity for all.\n\n## Organizer & Sponsors\n\n**Wisdomway Impact** connects mental wellbeing with community, social, and environmental resilience. We support leadership programs, community wellbeing strategies, and cross-sector impact projects that strengthen trust and collective care. We believe community wellbeing begins with inner wellbeing. Your ticket directly supports ongoing community initiatives and leadership development programs.\n**The Dais, Toronto Metropolitan University** is a public policy and leadership think tank, working at the intersection of technology, education and democracy to build shared prosperity and citizenship for Canada. With over 20 research reports exploring how AI is reshaping work, public policy, education and the nonprofit sector, the Dais has helped organizations build the knowledge and practical skills needed to adopt AI responsibly and effectively through the RAISE initiative which saw 550+ nonprofit professionals across Canada access practical training on AI governance and adoption.\n\n**GDG Toronto** is a chapter of Google Developer Groups, a global network of local, community-run developer groups. We bring people together around Google technologies through talks, hands-on workshops, and hackathons to be the technology literacy bridge for our community.","startDate":"2026-10-14T21:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-1-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Toronto Metropolitan University","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"350 Victoria St, Toronto, ON M5B 2K3, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Google Developer Group - Toronto","url":"https://www.meetup.com/gdg-toronto/"},"performer":"Google Developer Group - Toronto"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"TOPHATs Photography, Nutcrackers and New Zealand!?!","url":"https://www.meetup.com/beer-171/events/316748569/","description":"Join Lawrence, you top hatted host for an evening of New Zealand craft and culinary, followed by LUMINOUS 2026: A Photography Exhibit and then A Legacy in Motion: The National Ballet of Canada at 75.\n\nAt 5:30pm, we will meet at the patio upstairs at Hemmingways for our social. I'm going to have Boston Clam Chowder with their Sandwich of the Day, and wash it down with a Triple Bogey Lager.\n\nhttp://www.hemingways.to/\n142 Cumberland St, Toronto, ON M5R 1A8\n\nAt 6:30 pmish, we will pay our tabs and walk over to the Heliconian Club, to see their LUMINOUS 2026: A Photography Exhibit.\n\nLuminous Photographers: Linda Briskin, Brianna Caryll, Lucie Collins, Martha Davis, Kye Marshall, Denise Roberts, Jana Skarecky and Henrietta Walmark\n\nPerformers: Taivi, Brianna (Bri) Clarke, Kate Marshall Flaherty, Bianca Lakoseljac, Kye Marshall, Elizabeth Ruth, Jana Skarecky and JC Sulzenko\n\nGuest Photographers: Simone Creed, Grace Dan, Vivian East, Florence Guttman, Nola McConnan and Tanya Murdoch\n\nhttps://torontoheliconianclub.wildapricot.org/event-6747477\n35 Hazelton Ave, Toronto, ON M5R 2E3\n\nAt 7:30 mish, we will walk to the TD Gallery at the Toronto Reference Library, to see A Legacy in Motion: The National Ballet of Canada at 75.\n\nHighlights:\nStageworn costumes from Swan Lake, The Nutcracker and other popular ballets\nOver 40 original costume designs by nine designers\nVisual timeline of the history of The National Ballet of Canada\nVintage posters and programmes\nExamples of benesh notation (the choreography equivalent of sheet music)\nArchival photos, stage designs and more\n\nhttps://tpl.ca/programs-and-classes/exhibits/trl-exhibits/\n789 Yonge St Main Floor, Toronto, ON M4W 2G8","startDate":"2026-10-14T21:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Hemingway's Restaurant and Bar","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"142 Cumberland St, Toronto, ON M5R 1A8, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Beer Lovers","url":"https://www.meetup.com/beer-171/"},"performer":"Toronto Beer Lovers"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Beyond Chatbots: The AI Agent That Follows Up on Every Lead (Virtual)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ai-business-group/events/316470774/","description":"Every business has the same quiet leak: leads come in, and the busy ones slip through before you get back to them — and they call someone else.\n\nIn this session I'll show the whole journey live, on a real phone: a missed call triggers an instant text-back with a booking link, the lead books straight into the calendar, and the agent asks a few qualifying questions so you walk into the call prepared. We'll show you what's genuinely possible now, where it fits a real business, and what it would take to put it to work in yours.\n\nWe'll be using different tools including CRM, Excel, Claude Code & Cowork for demo purpose. You'll see how these tools figure things out for you and go beyond chatbots and conversation-based interaction. Essentially, you'll be building your own autonomous agent.\n\nWanna know more? Contact the host!","startDate":"2026-10-14T21:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-3-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Online- Virtual Classes","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"Online, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"AI & Business Group","url":"https://www.meetup.com/ai-business-group/"},"performer":"AI & Business Group"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Beginner Spanish Classes (In-Person)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/beginner-spanish-mississauga/events/316700094/","description":"**Spanish in Mississauga - Introduction to Spanish**\nNew beginner Spanish language classes in Mississauga\n\nIn this class, we will explore the Spanish language through 8 modules. We will cover basic concepts which you need to know in any Spanish-speaking country, and we will begin speaking right away and practicing in groups by module 3.\n\nThe goal is that you gain a basic understanding of the language. Weekly homework is required and active participation is encouraged.\n\n**These classes are not free.** Please consider watching an information session to learn more about the structure and how you can be part of this learning community.\n**Costs:** In-person registration can be made during the first class, and you can pay all classes at once without incurring payment fees (on this platform). You can also register for all classes right here on Eventbrite.\n\n**Date:** We will host weekly beginner Spanish classes weekly, for four (4) weeks:\n\n* October 7\n* October 14\n* October 21\n* October 28\n\nWe may offer a class social - practice in a group setting, restaurant or venue TBD.\nThis is your opportunity to learn language in only four classes!\n\n**Time**: Classes will begin at 5:30pm and will end at 6:30pm.\n\n**Location:** Mississauga Valley Community Centre\nClasses will be held in-person .\n\nPlease ensure that you participate in all four (4) classes, as we have already covered pronunciation and are practicing with our peers by class 2.\n\nIf you cannot attend all classes, consider joining us next month. We will continue to offer them on the first 4 Wednesdays of each month - participation in all classes is mandatory.\n\n**The instructor**\nMeet Rohit (Vic) Mehta- a fluent spanish speaker who has been a private tutor since 2014. He is continuing the popular Beginner Spanish Class series which was offered during pre-Covid times.\n\nWe hope to see you there! If you have any questions, please don't hesitate to contact us! Email dogoodspanish@gmail.com\n\n**Frequently Asked Questions:**\n\n**Do the classes have a cost?**\nYes, classes cost 20 each + fees (if paying online). You can also contribute cash or pay by interac e-transfer. There is an additional textbook available for purchase for 20.\n\n**How long are the classes?**\nClasses are held in-person for one (1) hour per week x 4 weeks. At the end of the weekly sessions, we will invite you to a social on a separate evening or weekend.\n\n**What should I bring?**\nA water bottle, snack, notebook and pen.\n\n**Is free parking available?**\nYes, the Mississauga Valley Community Centre has ample parking, and is also very accessible by transit.\n\n**Can I bring a friend?**\nYes absolutely, however all participants need to pay as an individual. We will credit you one (1) FREE class for bringing a friend.\n\n**Can I bring my kids?**\nNo, this is an adult only class. The themes are fast-paced and we want all participants to feel comfortable. We can make exceptions for older teenagers.\n\n**What if I miss a class?**\nIt is recommended that you attend all four (4) classes in the series. We can make a rare exception and offer a paid, Zoom class, for extreme circumstances.\n\n**What if I already took a beginner class?**\nConsider joining our Intermediate Class 4-part series, from 6:40pm to 7:40pm, beginning on the first Wednesday of each month.","startDate":"2026-10-14T21:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Mississauga Valley Community Centre, Hazel MacCallion Hall","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Mississauga","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1275 Mississauga Valley Blvd., ON L5A 3R8, Mississauga, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Beginner Spanish Mississauga","url":"https://www.meetup.com/beginner-spanish-mississauga/"},"performer":"Beginner Spanish Mississauga"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"French Meetup au Black Pony - $3","url":"https://www.meetup.com/frenchmeetup/events/316758644/","description":"(English below) Venez profiter de la bonne nourriture et d'une bonne conversation en français au café **Black Pony** situé au **1481 Gerrard St East.** Nous serons à l'arrière du café autour d'une grande table, prêts à vous accueillir.\n\nOn va pratiquer la langue de Molière tout en nous faisant de nouveaux amis(es)s. **Toutes les 30 minutes, nous changerons de place** pour favoriser les échanges. Tout le monde est le bienvenu, quel que soit son niveau.\n\nPour en savoir plus sur le café et son menu délicieux et varié : [https://www.blogto.com/restaurants/black-pony-toronto/](https://www.blogto.com/restaurants/black-pony-toronto/)\n\nSi vous ne souhaitez pas que votre photo soit publiée sur MeetUp, veuillez en informer Loren.\n\n**Pourquoi ces frais de 3$?** C'est pour payer le coût de l'hébergement sur la plate-forme Meetup pour l’année courante et les années précédentes. Nous vous demandons de payer $3.00 à chaque événement. Loren sera là pour recueillir vos contributions. Nous vous prions de bien vouloir apporter de la monnaie.\n\nSi vous préférez, vous pouvez utiliser ce lien pour payer sur Square: [CLIQUER ICI](https://square.link/u/S6dAAKd1)\n\nMerci,\n**Loren**\n\n..................................................................................................................\n\nCome and enjoy good food and good conversation at the **Black Pony café** located at **1481 Gerrard St East.** We'll be in the back of the café around a big table, ready to welcome you.\n\nWe'll be practicing the French language and making friends, **keeping in mind that every 45 minutes we'll be moving around to mix up the conversation.** Everyone is welcome, whatever your level.\n\nTo find out more about the cafe and its delicious and varied menu: https://www.blogto.com/restaurants/black-pony-toronto/\n\nWhy the $3 fee? It helps cover the cost of hosting the group on the Meetup platform for the current year and previous years. We ask participants to contribute **$3.00 at each event**. Loren will be there to collect contributions, so please bring change.\n\nIf you prefer, you can use this Square link:\n[CLICK HERE](https://square.link/u/S6dAAKd1)\n\nThank you,\nLoren","startDate":"2026-10-14T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"The Black Pony Café and Snack Bar","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1481 Gerrard St E, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Le French Meetup de Toronto - 3$","url":"https://www.meetup.com/frenchmeetup/"},"performer":"Le French Meetup de Toronto - 3$"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Coming Out, Being Out - Peer Discussion (Weekly)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/cobo-coming-out-being-out-peer-discussion-group/events/316700468/","description":"**Description**\n\nComing Out Being Out (COBO) is a peer discussion group that has served the LGBT community for over 15 years in downtown Toronto. We meet to share stories and opinions, challenges and triumphs at all stages of coming out and being out.\n\nCOBO participants are lesbian, gay, bisexual, transgender, two-spirit and questioning people. We welcome all who identify under the banner of queer sexual orientation and gender identity.\n\n**What We Do**\n\n\\|\\-\\| COBO participants are often seeking to:\n\n* Understand what experiences others have in coming out to family, friends and their respective communities.\n* Develop comfort in discussing their identity with others.\n* Meet others having the same experiences when it comes to living openly.\n* Receive the encouragement of peers.\n\n\\|\\-\\| Regular topics of discussion include:\n\n* How people choose to come out (at work, with family, with friends).\n* Where to find others like us in the community.\n* Challenges and triumphs in navigating family and partner relationships.\n\n**Where & When**\n\n* Every Wednesday from 6-8pm\n* Community meeting space at Casey House - 119 Isabella St., Toronto\n\n**How to Access the Meeting**\n\nRegistration on Meetup is not required to attend. Attendance is on a drop-in basis. The front door to our meeting space at Casey House is controlled by the main floor receptionist. To access the space when you arrive:\n\n* Press the button to the left of the main entrance door.\n* Tell the receptionist that you are there for the COBO meeting.\n* You will be buzzed in and someone from our group will come to show you to the meeting.\n\nWE LOOK FORWARD TO SEEING YOU ON WEDNESDAY!\n\n*COBO is a community group led by non-professional peer facilitators and is not a Casey House program.*","startDate":"2026-10-14T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Casey House - Community Meeting Space","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"119 Isabella Street, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"COBO - Peer Discussion Group","url":"https://www.meetup.com/cobo-coming-out-being-out-peer-discussion-group/"},"performer":"COBO - Peer Discussion Group"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Boxing Fundamentals (16+) — Build Strength & Skill | Fall 2026 Session","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-toronto-martial-arts-archery-dance/events/316700473/","description":"**Fall 2026 Session**\n**Registration required in advance**\n**[Register online](https://app.amilia.com/store/en/miles-nadal-jcc/api/Activity/Detail?activityId=xlZWnma)**\n☎️ Or call **416-924-6211 ext. 0**\n\n️ **Fees**\n• Full program session registration available\n• Prorated pricing if joining after the start date\n• Drop-in options may be available (space permitting)\n**Boxing Fundamentals (16+) at the Miles Nadal JCC**\n\nReady to build strength, sharpen your skills, and break a sweat? This no-contact beginner program introduces essential boxing fundamentals including stance, footwork, punches, bagwork, partner drills, and conditioning — all in a supportive and inclusive environment. No sparring involved.\n\nPerfect for new boxers or anyone looking to develop a strong foundation while improving fitness and confidence.\n\n**Led by Coach Nick Radionov — former Ukrainian National Olympic Boxing Team member, Level 3 Boxing Ontario–certified coach, and multi-time world kickboxing champion.**\n\n**Program Details**\n**Location:** Miles Nadal JCC — 750 Spadina Ave. (enter via Spadina doors)\n\n**What You’ll Learn & Benefit From**\n**Learn the Basics** — Develop proper form, movement, and striking technique\n**Build Strength & Stamina** — High-energy conditioning in every class\n**Train with Confidence** — Beginner-friendly instruction in a welcoming environment\n**Hands-On Skill Development** — Bagwork & partner drills (no-contact/no sparring)\n\n**What to Bring:** Handwraps, boxing gloves, indoor athletic shoes, and a water bottle.\n\nJoin us and build skill, strength, and confidence — one round at a time!","startDate":"2026-10-14T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Miles Nadal","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"750 Spadina Ave, Room 317b, M5S 2J2, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Downtown Toronto Martial Arts & Dance","url":"https://www.meetup.com/downtown-toronto-martial-arts-archery-dance/"},"performer":"Downtown Toronto Martial Arts & Dance"}]</script><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/7/e/4/4/highres_536252324.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/7/f/8/3/highres_536372643.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/c/0/d/2/highres_533149362.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/4/c/7/6/highres_513319574.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/e/4/b/f/highres_505678559.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/a/b/9/e/highres_535963934.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/4/0/8/f/highres_536356527.jpe